g for them  is the fact that they actually remain  within the bounds of truth  so it's always easier to tell the the  truth than to stick with a lie  over the long haul unless you're in a  terrorist society you know which is just  based on lies  because the truth actually does conform  to something real  and sooner or  this this person later fundamentally  motivated by  an appreciation for truth they think  that truth is in a certain  sense more encompassing more important  than their own self-image  for these other people something else is  more important  and when you place something else higher  on the scale than truth  you're really towing a dangerous line  and now aristotle doesn't develop this  as far as he  could the passages are fairly short  where he's discussing this  this is a very rich topic  that could be explored in much greater  detail

